+    # The accumulating variants of mulsh, at the same sop.  Same relationship
+    # to mulsh as mulua/mulus have to mulu: the halfword product is added to
+    # or subtracted from the hi:lo accumulator instead of being written to rz,
+    # which is why rz is unused here.  Used 16 times in the FFT butterfly
+    # kernels alone, where the sequence
+    #
+    #     muls rx, r3 ; mulshs a, b ; mulsha c, d ; mflo rz
+    #
+    # is one half of a complex multiply with Q15 twiddles.
